#X obj 639 8 chaos.logistic;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 754 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 A non-interpolating chaotic generator based on the logistic
map \, a one-dimensional discrete dynamical system. On each bang the
generator advances the map by one step and outputs the new x value.;
#X text 240 153 The map is defined by the difference equation:;
#X text 240 178 x[n+1] = λ * x[n] * (1 - x[n]);
#X obj 240 206 ui.link @background_color 0.90196 0.90196 0.90196
@title wiki: Logistic map @url
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Logistic_map;
#X text 240 227 Depending on the value of the parameter λ \, the map
demonstrates different types of behavior:;
#X text 240 267 • With λ between 0 and 1 \, the sequence eventually
decays to 0 \, regardless of the initial value;
#X text 240 307 • With λ between 1 and 2 \, the sequence quickly converges
to the value (λ − 1) / λ \, regardless of the initial value;
#X text 240 362 • With λ between 2 and 3 \, the sequence also eventually
converges to (λ − 1) / λ \, but first oscillates around that value
for some time;
#X text 240 417 • With λ between 3 and 1 + √6 ≈ 3.44949 \, from almost
any initial value the sequence settles into a stable oscillation between
two values (a period-2 cycle) \, which depend on λ;
#X text 240 487 • With λ between 3.44949 and 3.54409 (approximately)
\, from almost any initial value the sequence settles into a stable
oscillation among four values (period 4);
#X text 240 542 • As λ increases further \, the period doubles again
and again: 8 values \, then 16 \, 32 \, and so on — this is the period-doubling
cascade;
#X text 240 597 • At λ ≈ 3.56995 the onset of chaos occurs — the end
of the period-doubling cascade;
#X text 240 637 • For most λ values above 3.56995 \, the map shows
chaotic behavior \, but there are still isolated ranges of λ where
the behavior is non-chaotic (so-called periodic windows);
#X text 240 707 • Beyond λ = 4 \, almost all initial values eventually
leave the interval [0 \, 1] and diverge;
#X text 240 747 Because the values are not interpolated \, driving
the generator with a slow metro produces a stepped chaotic control
signal \, useful for driving filters \, pan positions or pitches.;
